## Composition with other classes

- **`:mm/Memory`** — memorial's `:mm.memory/links` enumerates the link entities extracted from its body
- **`:mm/Section`** — `:mm.link/in-section` references the containing section; section-level link queries follow
- **`:dt/Resource`** — `:mm.link/target-memory` references the target memorial for internal links

## Distinction from typed-edges

Markdown body links are NOT the same as frontmatter typed-edges:

- Typed-edges (cites, related, motivated-by, etc.) are SEMANTIC relations declared in frontmatter — substrate query surface
- Body links are NARRATIVE references — they document HOW memorials weave together in prose
- The two coexist; a memorial often has both

